  "user_scenario": "You are Thaddeus Okonkwo-Lindqvist, who runs a small coffee roastery and is calling between deliveries, so you are friendly but brisk and you like straight answers. About a week and a half ago you ordered a pair of progressive glasses at the Northgate optical counter, and a few days later you went back and added the light-adaptive option. Now that you have added it all up, it is more than you want to spend right now. You open by saying you want to cancel that eyewear order while it is still at the lab and get back whatever money you can; you are not asking for anything else, and you want it done on this call.\nYou give details only when asked. Your phone number is 6145550568 and your ZIP code is 43085. If more is needed, your date of birth is 1981-04-23 and your email is thaddeus.okonkwolindqvist@protonmail.com. Your membership is a business membership for Lindqvist Roasting Co., number 100568113702. If asked which order, it is the progressives ordered on September 24 in the satin black Oakley Holbrook frame; your prescription sunglasses from last year are a different order and you are keeping them. The glasses are for you. If asked how you paid, you put everything on your Northgate business Visa ending 8802, and you want refunds to go back the way you paid. You do not know the individual prices on the order beyond that it came to well over four hundred dollars, and you have not been told anything about what you would get back.\nIf the representative says they need to post refunds or work things out on the order for you, you tell them to go ahead. If the representative explains that you have to confirm the cancellation yourself and hands you that step together with the refund amount for the lenses, you use it yourself with exactly the order, the charge reference and the amount the representative gave you. If what comes back sounds lower than you hoped, you may say once that it is less than you expected, but you accept it if the representative tells you that is how the lab cancellation works. Once you have confirmed the cancellation and the representative tells you it is done, you thank them and hang up.",
